## Constraints and Security Protocols

A reliable developer tool must be transparent about its limitations and data handling practices.

*   **100% Client-Side Privacy:** This tool does not store, log, or transmit your code to any external servers. Everything runs entirely within your local browser session. You can safely paste proprietary code or test layouts without fear of data leakage.
*   **Volatile Memory:** Because the tool operates locally without requiring an account, your code is not saved across sessions. If you close the browser tab or refresh the page, your current workspace will be lost. Always copy your finalized code to a local file.
*   **Cross-Origin Restrictions:** For security reasons, the sandboxed environment may restrict certain advanced external API calls (CORS) or access to the parent window's local storage.

